    "text_full": "Cookie Settings\nMain Content\nMain Menu\nSEARCH\nMENU\nPeople\nPractices\nInsights\nPRESS RELEASE\nWiley Scores Several Top 10 Rankings in Vault’s 2027 Rankings\nLearn more\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\nA FOCUSED MINDSET\nWe're Wired In.\n\nWiley is wired into Washington. A nexus of influence renowned for navigating all branches of government, we seamlessly connect disciplines to adapt quickly to legal and regulatory shifts. Our impact is felt around the world through our dedication to staying ahead of the trends and fluent in the matters that matter most.\nMeet the Firm\n\nTrump Administration\nFAR and DFARS Overhaul\nArtificial Intelligence\nFeatured Insights\n\nWith a deep understanding of Washington and a broad knowledge of legal and regulatory frameworks, Wiley is well-positioned to deliver sharp analysis on the most pressing issues. These are our insights on the challenges shaping the business and regulatory landscape today and beyond.\n\nSubscribe\nView All\nITC Finds Unfairly Traded Imports of Container Chassis and Subassemblies from Mexico, Thailand, and Vietnam Injure the U.S. Industry\nPRESS RELEASE\nMay 20, 2026\nSeeds of Change: How Biotechnology is Reshaping Agriculture\nPODCAST\nMay 19, 2026\nATF Proposes Streamlining Machine Gun Transfer Procedures for Licensees\nALERT\nMay 18, 2026\nContractors Should Prepare as NIST Finalizes Enhanced Security Requirements for Protecting Controlled Unclassified Information\nALERT\nMay 15, 2026\nWiley Secures Major First Amendment Victory for Retail Energy Suppliers\nPRESS RELEASE\nMay 15, 2026\nPrevious\nSNAPSHOT OF IMPACT\nGreta M. Peisch\n\nGreta quoted by POLITICO regarding the Trump Administration's ongoing efforts to impose tariffs on U.S. imports.\n\nRead more\nGreta M. Peisch\nSNAPSHOT OF IMPACT\nIan L. Barlow\n\nIan discussed the implications of connected cars for consumers and regulatory actions on the Brookings Institution's TechTank Podcast.\n\nListen here\nNEXTAnn M. Begley\nSNAPSHOT OF IMPACT\nAnn